.TH ENCODE-BENCH 1 "2026-10-15" "encode-bench" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
encode-bench \- VMAF/SSIM/PSNR calibration bench for ffmpeg-encode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B encode-bench
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B encode-bench
encodes short samples of real files with a baseline (HEVC CQP) and a sweep of
AV1 CQP qualities, scores each against the source with libvmaf, SSIM and PSNR,
and reports size vs quality so you can pick the AV1 quality matching current
HEVC output.
.P
For ordinary video, a stream-copied segment is used as the reference. Animated
WebP sources are handled specially: they cannot be stream-copied into Matroska,
so the whole clip is decoded once to a lossless yuv420p reference (alpha
dropped) and the encode jobs use software decode plus
.B hwupload
because the VAAPI decoder cannot ingest WebP's argb/alpha format. The GPU still
performs the encode.
.P
VMAF runs with
.I n_subsample
(default 5): scoring every frame buffers the whole stream and peaks at several
GB of RAM. The tool reuses
.B ffmpeg-encode
own command builder, so it measures the exact pipeline the TUI uses.
Requires
.BR ffmpeg (1)
with libvmaf and a VAAPI device.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-t ", " \-\-seconds " SECONDS"
Sample length. Default: 30. Ignored for WebP, which always uses the whole clip.
.TP
.BI \-s ", " \-\-offset " OFFSET"
Sample start offset. Default: 5. Ignored for WebP.
.TP
.BI \-\-hevc\-quality " N"
HEVC baseline CQP quality. Default: 27.
.TP
.BI \-\-hevc\-values " N..."
Extra HEVC \-qp values to sweep.
.TP
.BI \-\-av1\-values " N..."
AV1 CQP \-global_quality values to sweep. Default:
.BR 90 " " 95 " " 97 " " 100 " " 105 .
.TP
.BI \-\-tolerance " N"
Allowed VMAF drop vs baseline. Default: 0.5.
.TP
.BI \-\-threads " N"
libvmaf threads. Default: half the CPUs.
.TP
.BI \-\-n\-subsample " N"
Score every Nth frame. Default: 5.
.TP
.B \-\-keep
Keep encoded samples instead of deleting them.
.SH EXAMPLES
Calibrate AV1 against one file:
.IP
.EX
encode-bench ~/Videos/sample.mkv
.EE
.P
Bench an animated WebP, sweeping both codecs:
.IP
.EX
encode-bench clip.webp \-\-hevc\-values 21 24 30 33 \\
    \-\-av1\-values 80 90 97 105 115 125
.EE
.P
Note that
.BR \-\-hevc\-values " and " \-\-av1\-values
consume all following integers, so list the files before the options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Completed.
.TP
.B 1
No VAAPI device found, or a sample failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg-encode (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
